From: LuneOS port <webos-ports@webos-ports.org>
Subject: [PATCH] q linker: restore legacy StaticTlsLayout::finish_layout()

The android16-tls rework split StaticTlsLayout into an
ANDROID_VERSION_MAJOR >= 16 variant and a legacy one, but only the new
variant kept a finish_layout() definition. The legacy class still
declares it and linker_tls.cpp still calls it, so every headers < 16
build produces a q.so with an undefined
_ZN15StaticTlsLayout13finish_layoutEv and hybris dies on the first
property_get:

  ERROR: Failed to load hybris linker for Android SDK version 30:
  /usr/lib/libhybris/linker/q.so: undefined symbol:
  _ZN15StaticTlsLayout13finish_layoutEv

Nothing caught it at build time because a shared object may carry
undefined symbols until dlopen. Restore the upstream bionic Q
implementation on the legacy field names.

Upstream-Status: Pending [belongs on Herrie82/libhybris herrie/android16-tls]
---
--- a/common/q/bionic/libc/bionic/bionic_elf_tls.cpp
+++ b/common/q/bionic/libc/bionic/bionic_elf_tls.cpp
@@ -157,6 +157,15 @@
   if (value < old_value) overflowed_ = true;
   return value;
 }
+
+void StaticTlsLayout::finish_layout() {
+  // Round the offset up to the alignment.
+  offset_ = round_up_with_overflow_check(offset_, alignment_);
+  if (overflowed_ || offset_ > MAX_SIZE) {
+    async_safe_fatal("error: TLS segments in static TLS overflowed (size %zu, max %zu)",
+                     offset_, MAX_SIZE);
+  }
+}
 #endif
 
 // Copy each TLS module's initialization image into a newly-allocated block of
